================================================================================
Algorithms distilled into native Go (clean-room, NO source code used)
================================================================================

The following projects inspired ideas that were re-authored from scratch in Go.
No source code from them is included in or distributed with Prefex. These are
courtesy credits, not license obligations:

  - RouteLLM            (Apache-2.0)  https://github.com/lm-sys/RouteLLM
  - LLMLingua / -2      (MIT)         https://github.com/microsoft/LLMLingua
  - caveman-compression (MIT)         https://github.com/wilpel/caveman-compression
  - RTK                 (Apache-2.0)  https://github.com/rtk-ai/rtk
  - Mem0                (Apache-2.0)  https://github.com/mem0ai/mem0
  - MemGPT / Letta      (Apache-2.0)  https://github.com/letta-ai/letta
  - OpenHands           (MIT, core)   https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands
  - GraphRAG            (MIT)         https://github.com/microsoft/graphrag
  - vLLM                (Apache-2.0)  https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm
  - Ollama              (MIT)         https://github.com/ollama/ollama
  - headroom            (Apache-2.0)  https://github.com/headroomlabs-ai/headroom
      (algorithms reimplemented in Go: content-routed compaction, recover-on-demand
       CCR, output shaping. The headroom Kompress *model* is run via the optional
       sidecar below, not reimplemented.)
  - codeburn            (MIT)         https://github.com/getagentseal/codeburn
      (ideas: dead-MCP-tool detection thresholds, cache-aware waste pricing, the
       embedded-pricing-snapshot approach. Re-authored as Setup Health.)
  - Invariant Scanner   (Apache-2.0)  https://github.com/invariantlabs-ai/invariant
      (idea: typed violation taxonomy for agent tool-call traces. Re-authored as
       the live policy gateway's Rego policy bundle; theirs is post-hoc trace
       analysis, ours gates on the wire.)
  - Storybloq           (PolyForm Shield 1.0.0)  https://github.com/Storybloq/storybloq
      (idea: structured session handover — goal/progress/files/blockers/next
       persisted per project across sessions. Schema shape distilled from public
       docs only; no source code used.)

================================================================================
Third-party components bundled or invoked by the OPTIONAL Kompress sidecar
================================================================================

These apply ONLY if you opt into the text-compaction sidecar
(compression.kompress: true). The sidecar runs out of process; the Prefex
binary itself stays model-free. See deploy/kompress-sidecar/.

  headroom / Kompress (model + ONNX inference run by the sidecar)
    headroom's algorithms are reimplemented in Go (credited above); this entry
    is the keep/drop model the sidecar runs.
    License: Apache-2.0
    https://github.com/headroomlabs-ai/headroom

  chopratejas/kompress-v2-base
    ModernBERT keep/drop model weights served by the sidecar (downloaded from
    Hugging Face at deploy time; not redistributed by Prefex).
    License: Apache-2.0
    https://huggingface.co/chopratejas/kompress-v2-base

  ModernBERT (answerdotai/ModernBERT-base)
    The base encoder the kompress weights are fine-tuned from.
    License: Apache-2.0
    https://github.com/AnswerDotAI/ModernBERT

  ONNX Runtime
    Inference runtime for the model (no PyTorch).
    License: MIT
    https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime

  Hugging Face Transformers
    Tokenization for the sidecar.
    License: Apache-2.0
    https://github.com/huggingface/transformers

================================================================================
Third-party Go libraries compiled into the prefex binary
================================================================================

These are linked into the released binary and distributed with it:

  github.com/open-policy-agent/opa  (Apache-2.0)    embedded policy engine (policy gateway)
  github.com/redis/go-redis/v9   (BSD-2-Clause)    optional Redis session store
  gopkg.in/yaml.v3               (MIT, Apache-2.0)  config parsing
  modernc.org/sqlite             (BSD-3-Clause)     embedded dashboard database

The complete set of third-party Go modules compiled into the binary (45 modules,
direct and transitive — the growth over the earlier 22 is OPA's dependency
tree) and their licenses is listed in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md.

Embedded data:

  LiteLLM model_prices_and_context_window.json  (MIT)
    https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm — the model-pricing snapshot embedded in
    the binary and refreshed per release / via `prefex pricing refresh`.

